{
  "$comment": [
    "Named regions as explicit state sets.",
    "'New England' appears in no data source, so colloquial regions are defined here as data",
    "rather than left to the model to interpret. That keeps region queries reproducible: the",
    "same question returns the same airport set every time, and the definition is auditable.",
    "Metro-level questions ('LA airports', 'Bay Area') are handled by proximity search against",
    "airport coordinates instead, because metro areas do not map onto state boundaries."
  ],
